<article class="env-lemma" id="0D73">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D73">Lemma <span data-tag="0D73">85.6.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/09WE" data-tag="09WE">85.3.3</a>. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a sheaf of rings on $\mathcal{C}_{total}$. If $\mathcal{I}$ is injective in $\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O})$, then $\mathcal{I}_ n$ is a totally acyclic sheaf on $\mathcal{C}_ n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0D6Y" data-tag="0D6Y">21.37.4</a> applied to the inclusion functor $\mathcal{C}_ n \to \mathcal{C}_{total}$ and its properties proven in Lemma <a href="/tag/09WG" data-tag="09WG">85.3.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>